Total Changes: 157

[IMP] hr: make the Working Schedule required on employees

making hr.version.resource_calendar_id required and redefining a
"flexible" employee as one assigned a calendar of the new 'undefined'
type with no predefined slots, instead of having no calendar at all.
resource.resource.calendar_id becomes required the same way.

* resource: hours_per_week/hours_per_day move onto resource.calendar
  as the single source of truth; resource.mixin's own copies
  (inherited by hr.employee, mrp.workcenter, appointment.resource)
  are removed.

* is_flexible/is_fully_flexible drop from stored/related Boolean
  fields to plain _is_flexible()/_is_fully_flexible() methods.

* hr.employee._is_flexible()/_is_fully_flexible() gain an optional
  `date` argument (defaulting to today, same as before) so callers
  that already have a real target date - leave requests, attendance
  overtime, planning slots, timesheets, appointments - resolve
  flexibility against the version/calendar that was actually active
  on that date instead of implicitly against today's.

* hr.employee._get_unusual_days() now passes the employee's resource
  to resource.calendar._get_unusual_days() for flexible employees,
  so only actual leave days are greyed out instead of an arbitrary
  fixed weekly pattern borrowed from the company calendar.

* hr.employee._get_calendar_attendances()/_get_expected_attendances()
  drop their flexible-employee fallback to the company calendar and
  use the employee's/version's own calendar unconditionally.

* resource.calendar._get_attendance_intervals_days_data() is fixed to
  split attendance intervals per calendar day before bucketing them,
  instead of assuming every interval fits within a single day - an
  assumption a fully flexible calendar's multi-day synthesized
  interval breaks, previously collapsing an arbitrarily long span to
  exactly one day.

